WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.022 --> 00:00:04.605
- At least 49 dead.

00:00:05.497 --> 00:00:06.911
- 53 injured.

00:00:06.911 --> 00:00:09.023
- Hundreds of lives changed forever

00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:10.550
and not for the better.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.384
- But we know this story.

00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:14.500
- At what point do we add this to our

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.125
list of proud American traditions?

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:18.999
- I don't know.

00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:21.248
- I hate to argue, I hate rolling my eyes

00:00:21.248 --> 00:00:23.147
at people that I respect.

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:25.804
Hate leaving a conversation
only feeling worse.

00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:27.296
So I'll stay out of it.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:31.622
- [Voiceover] But at least
49 dead and 53 injured.

00:00:31.622 --> 00:00:33.452
- There are too many dark days.

00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:35.074
Too many heavy hearts.

00:00:35.074 --> 00:00:36.528
Too many bodies.

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:38.177
- Too many bodies.

00:00:38.177 --> 00:00:40.104
- And I don't know.

00:00:40.104 --> 00:00:42.876
I watched my brothers and sisters fall.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.914
- [Voiceover] I turn on the news.

00:00:43.914 --> 00:00:47.004
I try to understand but
we fight and we argue.

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:48.319
- [Voiceover] And nobody is to blame

00:00:48.319 --> 00:00:49.731
and everybody is to blame.

00:00:49.731 --> 00:00:50.761
- Machines are to blame.

00:00:50.761 --> 00:00:52.522
- Healthcare is to blame.

00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:53.963
- Gods are to blame.

00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:55.463
- We are to blame.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.287
But we aren't doing anything.

00:01:01.598 --> 00:01:03.937
- We throw opinions like punches.

00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:06.034
- Spilling out of our mouths like blood

00:01:06.034 --> 00:01:07.784
with our last breath.

00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:10.652
But nobody listens.

00:01:10.652 --> 00:01:12.018
- Nothing changes.

00:01:12.018 --> 00:01:13.781
- [Voiceover] And it happens again.

00:01:13.781 --> 00:01:14.649
- [Voiceover] And again.

00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:15.663
- [Voiceover] And again.

00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:17.079
- And again.

00:01:17.079 --> 00:01:19.329
- So tell me, what do I do?

00:01:20.423 --> 00:01:22.681
- Do I sign or donate?

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.856
Give my blood or my tears?

00:01:24.856 --> 00:01:26.869
And what is any of it doing?

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:28.393
- What are we doing?

00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:29.658
- I don't know.

00:01:29.658 --> 00:01:32.470
- This is not a time for getting defensive

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.518
or being offended.

00:01:34.518 --> 00:01:36.276
You know what?

00:01:36.276 --> 00:01:38.049
I am offended.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:40.583
- I'm offended that our
children are growing up

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:43.166
in a world afraid of going to school

00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:45.195
or the movies or the club.

00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:47.302
- That places meant to help us grow

00:01:47.302 --> 00:01:51.295
as individuals are being
turned into graveyards.

00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:53.996
- I am offended that
this is our new normal.

00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:57.428
There is nothing normal about this.

00:01:57.428 --> 00:01:58.261
- And yet.

00:01:59.392 --> 00:02:01.422
Active shooter in Texas.

00:02:01.422 --> 00:02:03.535
- [Voiceover] A family
murdered in New Mexico.

00:02:03.535 --> 00:02:05.694
- [Voiceover] Seven
mothers mourn in Chicago.

00:02:05.694 --> 00:02:07.541
- [Voiceover] Another
child loss in Maryland.

00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:09.474
- [Voiceover] Two more lives in Florida.

00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:10.451
- [Voiceover] Another in New York.

00:02:10.451 --> 00:02:11.444
- [Voiceover] Another in Louisiana.

00:02:11.444 --> 00:02:12.799
- [Voiceover] Another in Arkansas

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.966
and that was just one day.

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:18.812
- I am tired of talking.

00:02:18.812 --> 00:02:22.979
Tired of praying, tired of
wet cheeks and raw eyes.

00:02:24.015 --> 00:02:25.098
- I am tired.

00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:28.567
- I'm tired.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.870
- Do we love freely or restrict freedom?

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.843
- Do we change our laws or
acknowledge our illnesses?

00:02:34.843 --> 00:02:36.881
- Do we crack down or straighten up?

00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:39.984
- Or maybe, do we do all of the above?

00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:42.317
- Because I don't know much.

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:45.849
But I know I've had enough.

